{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the daughter of the king of the Negev:</b> She is the Queen of Sheba, and this kingdom is called in the language of Ishmael Eliman, and to this day a woman rules over them, and it is under the authority of the king of Egypt to this day. And this Sheba — it is opposite the Negev, opposite the land of Israel. And this matter is known in the books, and I have forgotten their names." "<b>And the meaning of 'to make equity':</b> Peace between the kings. And behold, the king of the North wanted to take her for himself as a wife." "<b>'He shall not retain the strength of the arm':</b> And the king of Egypt shall take her by force, and shall also take her guardian and the astrologers who were with her, and this is: 'and she who bore him' [etc.]."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra appears to refer to a contemporary female ruler of a region in the Arabian Peninsula under Egyptian sovereignty; 'Eliman' may be a toponym otherwise unattested and possibly corrupt.", 2 "The phrase 'and this is: ומחזיקה בעתים' appears truncated or garbled; rendered hyper-literally as Ibn Ezra's shorthand linking the verse's phrase to his interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:59.432885604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}